the mnu kernel ChangeLog   - version 0.12
    - Release date: 2026-08-17
    - Release creator: tas0dev

Changes:
* Hardened KPTI entry and return paths for syscalls,
  interrupts, and exceptions on x86_64.
* Isolated per-CPU descriptor tables and syscall state
  from user page tables.
* Fixed fork page-table cloning and user-context restore.
* Added SMP startup, service scheduling, and secondary
  CPU preemption.
* Hardened scheduler context switching and preserved
  SIMD and FS-base state across switches.
* Added process credentials and enforced UID, GID, and
  Unix file mode checks.
* Added application-scoped storage and capability-scoped
  settings storage.
* Added path-based read, write, create, delete, list, and
  execute authorization.
* Hardened IPC reply routing, endpoint generations, and
  sender identity resolution.
* Separated IPC shared-page mappings from process heaps.
* Added secure random generation and validated UTC time.
* Added ext2 writes, lstat, rename, rmdir, pipe fixes,
  and batched filesystem I/O.
* Added execve, fork inheritance, process environments,
  and POSIX spawn support.
* Added PlugKit virtio PCI discovery, transport, DMA,
  and virtqueue support.
* Added framebuffer, DMA, and MMIO mapping interfaces with
  allocator-owned RAM rejection.
* Moved executable signature policy to user services and
  retained a bootstrap execution allowlist.
* Added user-process permission enforcement and secure UI
  capability definitions.
* Improved service startup wakeups and process inspection.
